CFG659: does the settling field P leave any signature in ordinary matter or light?

Criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md (committed alone, 75e95fe06). Reading lane on CFG694 (action), CFG695 (saturating W), CFG696
(radiative attractor); no CFG690-699 file is edited or imported.
  L = -|grad Phi - 4 pi G lam P|^2 / 8 pi G - rho_b Phi - W(P) - (gamma/2)|grad P|^2 + (I/2)|P_t|^2      (lam = 1 is the action)
  gamma = 2 pi G L*^2  (CFG691: l_gamma = L*^2 / 2 r_M);  c_P = sqrt(gamma / I) unfixed (CFG696).
  W: CFG695 saturating vacuum minus the critical quadratic; in u = 4 pi G P:  4 pi G W = w(u) = -a0 u - a0^2 ln(1 - u/a0) - u^2/2,
     w'(u) = u^2/(a0 - u),  w''(u) = u(2 a0 - u)/(a0 - u)^2.   Local gap for P perturbations: m^2 = 4 pi G w''/gamma = 2 w''/L*^2.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED; footings 9.3603e-11 / 1.1312e-10 never pooled; cold energy mass required; no particle species; not
"theory closed"; no LCDM or standard-MOND yardstick in any verdict.

Run:  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 nice -n 10 python3 cfg659.py        (CFG659_MUTATE=1: lam = 0; exit 1 iff any channel is non-zero)

D1  coupling: Phi equation div(grad Phi - 4 pi G lam P) = 4 pi G rho_b  =>  g = g_N - 4 pi G lam P_L;  P_T never enters Phi
  [PASS] D1 g = g_N - 4piG lam P_L exactly; a purely transverse P leaves Phi unchanged: max|g - (g_N - 4piG lam P_L)| = 9.0e-16; max|Phi[P_T] - Phi_N| = 2.3e-13
    Matter feels P ONLY through Phi (universal, composition-blind): a passing longitudinal wave gives delta a = -4 pi G lam delta P_L.
    Electromagnetism: the action has NO term containing A_mu or F_munu. Any direct P-light coupling would be a NEW TERM (a knob);
    none is added. Light sees P only through the metric potentials (Phi; Psi = Phi is the open relativistic completion).

D2  linear waves about a background u0 (a0 = footing):
    longitudinal:  I w^2 = gamma (k^2 + m^2),  m^2 = 2 w''(u0)/L*^2   (the |grad Phi - 4piG P|^2 term is P_L-independent: no mass)
    transverse:    I w^2 = gamma k^2 + 4 pi G lam^2 + gamma m_T^2         (massive, and decoupled from matter by D1)
    speed c_P = sqrt(gamma/I) (unfixed, CFG696). These are NOT GR gravitational waves: longitudinal, speed c_P, gapped where u0 != 0.
    regimes: deep (u0 << a0) m^2 = 4 u0/(a0 L*^2);  saturated (g >> a0) m ~ sqrt2 g/(a0 L*);  screened core of a star: u0 ~ GM/L*^2 ~ 0.
D3  traveling longitudinal wave: e = I Pdot^2, flux F = c_P e;  delta u0 = 4 pi G lam delta P0 = lam sqrt(16 pi G c_P F)/(w L*)

K1  static field energy of CFG696's functional (cubic W): E_code(S) = -int_0^S [v'^2/2 + v^2/s^2 + |v|^3/(3s) - v/s] ds
  [PASS] K1 E_code(200) = CFG696 released energy for the zero start (2.99995) within 2%: E_code(200) = 3.00331; E_code(1e4) = 5.6058; d E/d ln S = 0.6654 (deep-regime analytic 2/3)

S1  energy released by settling, saturating W (framework-native): E = M_b V_f^2 * eps(R/r_M),  V_f^4 = G M_b a0, r_M = sqrt(G M_b/a0)
    canonical galaxy : V_f    165 km/s, r_M    9.5 kpc, R/r_M  10.6, eps 2.076, E 6.76e+51 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 2.1e+34 W, merging (R/V_f = 0.59 Gyr) 3.6e+35 W
    canonical group  : V_f    334 km/s, r_M   38.6 kpc, R/r_M  13.0, eps 2.207, E 4.89e+53 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 1.5e+36 W, merging (R/V_f = 1.46 Gyr) 1.1e+37 W
    canonical cluster: V_f   1056 km/s, r_M  385.9 kpc, R/r_M   5.2, eps 1.624, E 3.60e+56 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 1.1e+39 W, merging (R/V_f = 1.85 Gyr) 6.2e+39 W
    alt       galaxy : V_f    173 km/s, r_M    8.6 kpc, R/r_M  11.6, eps 2.137, E 7.65e+51 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 2.4e+34 W, merging (R/V_f = 0.56 Gyr) 4.3e+35 W
    alt       group  : V_f    350 km/s, r_M   35.1 kpc, R/r_M  14.2, eps 2.268, E 5.53e+53 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 1.8e+36 W, merging (R/V_f = 1.40 Gyr) 1.3e+37 W
    alt       cluster: V_f   1107 km/s, r_M  351.0 kpc, R/r_M   5.7, eps 1.683, E 4.10e+56 J; no-trap ceiling L: relaxed (10 Gyr) 1.3e+39 W, merging (R/V_f = 1.77 Gyr) 7.4e+39 W
    cosmic ceiling (CFG630 K4 max d rho_DE/rho_DE0 = 5.87e-06): all settling energy ever, as P waves: u_P <= 3.09e-15 J/m^3

S2  trapping: baryon-driven settling at w = 2 pi / t (t = 10 Gyr relaxed, R/V_f merging) below the local gap is evanescent;
    tau = int_R^r_out sqrt(m^2 - w^2/c_P^2) dr (point-mass law background); radiated fraction <= exp(-2 tau). Minimum over the window:
    canonical galaxy : min tau 270 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-234
    canonical group  : min tau 237 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-205
    canonical cluster: min tau 2.17e+03 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-1.89e+03
    alt       galaxy : min tau 257 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-223
    alt       group  : min tau 225 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-195
    alt       cluster: min tau 2.06e+03 (merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c) -> radiated fraction <= 10^-1.79e+03

S3  CFG696 PDE, code units: start static, ramp the baryon source 1 -> 1.1 over T (smooth), run T + 600; radiated = flux out at S = 200
    T =    0: radiated +1.4247e-02  (1.00e+00 of the step)
    T =    3: radiated +1.0814e-02  (7.59e-01 of the step)
    T =   10: radiated +5.8976e-03  (4.14e-01 of the step)
    T =   30: radiated +1.4042e-03  (9.86e-02 of the step)
    T =  100: radiated +3.8124e-05  (2.68e-03 of the step)
    T =  300: radiated +8.6811e-06  (6.09e-04 of the step)
    slope d ln E_rad / d ln T over T = 30..300: -2.21  (step -> slow: adiabatic suppression)
    physical T in code units = t_phys c_P / l_gamma; a 0.6-10 Gyr settling at c_P >= 5e-3 c, l_gamma <= 0.1 pc gives T >= 1e9.

=== CHANNELS (worst corner of L* x c_P, each footing; verdict on the worst)

C1  gas heating. D5: I w^2 = gamma(k^2+m^2) - (4piG lam)^2 rho_b / w^2 (responsive baryons); absorbed fraction per radian
    <= w_J^2 W_I^2 / w^4 (W_I^2 = 4 pi G/I); heating per unit mass h = 4 pi G W_I^2 F / (w^3 c_P), taken at the lowest propagating w = c_P m.
    cluster ICM      : cooling 7.23e-07 W/kg; worst corner (alt, L_merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c): no-trap ceiling h 3.93e-09 W/kg (5.4e-02 of 0.1 x cooling); with trapping 0.0e+00 -> BELOW THRESHOLD
    galactic hot halo: cooling 1.45e-08 W/kg; worst corner (alt, L_merging, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c): no-trap ceiling h 4.46e-10 W/kg (3.1e-01 of 0.1 x cooling); with trapping 2.5e-233 -> BELOW THRESHOLD

C2  disc heating, solar neighbourhood (R0 = 8 kpc, galaxy halo of S1). Stars are collisionless and w >= c_P m >> orbital frequencies,
    so the linear secular heating is zero (adiabatic); the number below is the D5 full-dissipation ceiling.
    threshold 0.1 x sigma_z^2/10 Gyr = 1.27e-10 W/kg; worst (alt, L_merging, L* 1000.0, c_P 0.005 c): ceiling 2.56e-10 W/kg (2.0e+00); forced oscillation dv 5.34e+01 m/s; with trapping 1.4e-233 -> BELOW THRESHOLD

C3  quadrupole P radiation from a binary in its screened core (sigma = 2 r_M^2/L*^2 << 1: linear; local gap from the Galaxy's u0):
    chi = div P obeys chi_tt/c_P^2 - lap chi = 4 pi G lam rho_b/gamma; flux c_P gamma chi^2 =>  Pow = G lam^2 (Idd_ii^2 + 2 Idd:Idd)/(30 L*^2 c_P^3)
    circular orbit: Pow/Pow_GR = lam^2 (1/12) (c/c_P)^3 (c/(w_orb L*))^2.  Double pulsar: P_b = 2.4545 h (e = 0.088 neglected).
    L*    5.75 pc: ratio c_P 0.005c: 3.8e-06, c_P 0.015c: 1.4e-07, c_P 0.1c: 4.7e-10, c_P 1.0c: 4.7e-13   | room 9e-5 excludes c_P < 1.7e-03 c
    L*  100.00 pc: ratio c_P 0.005c: 1.2e-08, c_P 0.015c: 4.6e-10, c_P 0.1c: 1.6e-12, c_P 1.0c: 1.6e-15   | room 9e-5 excludes c_P < 2.6e-04 c
    L* 1000.00 pc: ratio c_P 0.005c: 1.2e-10, c_P 0.015c: 4.6e-12, c_P 0.1c: 1.6e-14, c_P 1.0c: 1.6e-17   | room 9e-5 excludes c_P < 5.6e-05 c
    binary sigma = 2.3e-04 (screened, linear); v_orb/c_P at the floor = 0.42 (slow-motion OK); all corners propagate (2w >> c_P m_gap): True
    worst corner 3.8e-06 vs room 9e-5 -> BELOW THRESHOLD (4.2e-02)

C4  nHz band. Settling at w ~ 1/t_dyn is ~7 decades below the band and trapped (S2): no settling signal in band.
    SMBH binary (1e9 Msun, f_GW 1e-8 Hz): free ratio as C3; the binary sits where g_N ~ 1e9 a0, sigma = 2 r_M^2/L*^2 > 2,
    so the saturated vacuum (u -> a0) is NOT screened (stiffness shifts the source by 1 - 2/sigma); gap m = sqrt(2 w''(u))/L*.
    a_bin = 0.017 pc; largest FREE ratio 1.9e+03 at canonical|5.75|0.005 (gap/w at source 1.0e+06, tau 2.20e+07)
    min tau over window 1.90e+04; worst ESCAPED ratio 0.0e+00 (canonical|5.75|0.005) -> BELOW THRESHOLD
    local propagation at the Sun needs w > c_P m(u0): band edge 2pi x 2 nHz vs gap 6.2e-09 s^-1 (c_P = c, L* 5.75)

C5  merging cluster (Bullet-like: M_b 1e14, v 4500 km/s, R 500 kpc). Below the gap the response is in phase (no dissipation but
    trapped radiation): fractional profile change (w/w_m)^2 with w = v/R; even-in-v, so no centroid shift. Ceiling if fully damped: v/w_m.
    worst (alt, L* 1000.0 pc, c_P 0.005 c): profile change 6.1e-06 (vs 0.05: BELOW THRESHOLD, 1.2e-04); offset 0.0e+00 kpc (BELOW THRESHOLD); fully-damped ceiling 1.23 kpc (0.12 of 10 kpc)
    NOTE: v_bulk 4500 km/s > c_P at the 5e-3 c floor: True -> the c_P floor must sit above bulk speeds (Cherenkov), a consistency bound, not a signature.

C6  light: no P-photon term in the action -> REQUIRES NEW COUPLING (not added). Via gravity (if Psi = Phi), the cosmic ceiling
    P-wave energy (u_P 3.1e-15 J/m^3, at the lowest propagating w) gives dPhi/c^2 <= 1.3e-09 (time-varying; vs 1e-5 CMB-level anisotropy: BELOW THRESHOLD, 1.3e-04); trapping removes even this.

